{
  "$schema-note": "Who may reach each route, as data. Checked live by test/authz_matrix.test.ts: every route in Fastify's inventory must have exactly one row, every row must name a live route, and each of the four callers (anonymous, user, moderator, admin) is sent to each route — a caller the row admits must get past the authentication and role gate, a caller it excludes must be stopped by that gate and nothing later. Widening a route (a moderator reaching an admin action) fails CI naming the route. 'who' is the coarse gate the server enforces before the handler runs; 'scope' is the finer ownership or state rule the handler enforces afterwards and which test/idor.test.ts and test/authz_fuzz.test.ts cover.",
  "who": {
    "public": "no session needed",
    "account": "any signed-in account (user, moderator, admin)",
    "staff": "moderator or admin",
    "admin": "admin only",
    "worker": "the payout worker's bearer token; every browser session is refused"
  },
